{
  "summary": "Intel's Gaudi 3 splits work between two kinds of engine: eight large matrix-multiply engines (MMEs, each a 256×256 systolic array) and 64 programmable Tensor Processor Cores (TPCs) for everything else. Two 5 nm compute dies share 96 MB of on-die SRAM, 128 GB of HBM2e and 24 integrated 200 GbE RoCE ports for scale-out without separate NICs.",
